  "mathematical_target": "For every positive finite dimension and arbitrary complex square matrix X, if every genuine Hermitian positive-semidefinite block completion [A X; X* B] has complex Euclidean operator norm at most that of A+B, then X is an affine complex combination of an actual Hermitian matrix and the identity. This is the full original necessity implication, with the universal A/B premise, singular completions, zero/scalar matrices, repeated values, and dimensions one and two retained. No converse or genericity assumption is claimed.",
